results.root_cause_summary:
The session exhibits a classic "unconstrained long-form reasoning without tool use" failure mode. The agent:
    (1) Never invokes any computational tool, relying entirely on error-prone manual arithmetic;
    (2) Reasons in circles, re-deriving the same results 3-5 times instead of proving once by induction;
    (3) Fails to converge, oscillating on whether the partition is unique;
    (4) Likely hits the context window limit mid-reasoning, leaving the second problem's conclusion incomplete.
    The core issue is absence of a verification loop (no code execution) combined with no self-imposed brevity discipline, leading to ~88% redundancy and a truncated, low-confidence outcome.
